//
// 4-byte events; file order [b0,b1,b2,b3], b3 = opcode (>=0x80 cmd, <0x80 note).
// NOTE: b0=velocity, b1=gate% (ngg), b2=note length (ngs), b3=note. 0xD2=tone
// select (sample index=b2). Duration is ngs; gate>=100 avoids the SE release-clamp.
//
// TWO OUTPUT TARGETS:
//  • Export blob.h  — for a decomp project that recompiles (surgical text splice).
//  • Patch EXE      — for an already-compiled game: the sequences compile to the
//    identical bytes, so we search the executable for each cue's stock byte
//    signature and patch the edited bytes in place. No source needed.
//
// Auto-link: WVX_swap calls SE_autoLengthen(indices, ratio).
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

